{
  "requirement": "`habeas setup` MUST configure native nextest settings in\n`.config/nextest.toml` at the Cargo workspace root so the coverage workflow of\n{cite}`requirements.test-coverage.run` routes each executed test attempt through\nthe per-process collector of {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.processes`.\nThose settings MUST use nextest's own configuration format.\nRepeating setup MUST avoid duplicate configuration, preserve unrelated nextest\nsettings, and report conflicting settings for review rather than overwrite them.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the marked tests adequate for `requirements.test-coverage.setup.configuration`. The obligations and their tests are below.\n\n**Placement at the workspace root.**\n- `configuration.rs#mod[tests]/fn[workspace_member_uses_the_native_config_at_the_workspace_root]` runs `configure` from a workspace member. It asserts the path is the root's `.config/nextest.toml` and that no `.config` or `target` appears in the member.\n- The same test covers an excluded member, where the member is its own root.\n- `fn[explicit_workspace_pointer_places_configuration_at_a_sibling_workspace]` covers an explicit `workspace = '../workspace'` pointer.\n\n**Routing every attempt through the collector, in nextest's own format.**\n- `configure` ends by running `check` on the content it plans to write, so a generated config must satisfy `check`. `check` requires:\n  - `experimental` to include `wrapper-scripts`;\n  - `scripts.wrapper.habeas-coverage` with command `habeas coverage-process` and `target-runner = \"within-wrapper\"`;\n  - an unconditional first `run-wrapper` rule with filter `all()` and no platform.\n- `fn[native_settings_inheritance_and_precedence]` checks the generated source against profile inheritance, rule precedence, a platform-restricted rule, a filter-restricted rule, and a self-inheriting profile. It also checks that corrupting `coverage-process` or `within-wrapper` is rejected.\n- `tests/setup.rs#fn[coverage_setup_is_idempotent_and_hook_needs_no_coverage_chapter]` asserts the file written by the real `habeas setup` binary contains `coverage-process`.\n- Several tests in `tests/execution_coverage.rs` run real nextest against the generated config. They are not marked for this requirement, but they back up the native-format claim. The marked tests alone check the format only through `check`.\n\n**Repeating setup avoids duplicates.**\n- `fn[native_settings_inheritance_and_precedence]` asserts a second `configure` returns identical source.\n- `tests/setup.rs#fn[coverage_setup_is_idempotent_and_hook_needs_no_coverage_chapter]` runs `habeas setup` twice and asserts the config file is byte-identical.\n\n**Preserving unrelated settings.**\n- `fn[native_settings_inheritance_and_precedence]` starts from a config with `experimental = ['setup-scripts']`, `retries = 2` and a `setup` script rule. It asserts all three survive in the planned output.\n- `tests/setup.rs#fn[coverage_setup_preserves_custom_index_and_preflights_conflicts]` covers preserving unrelated book files.\n\n**Reporting conflicts without overwriting.**\n- `fn[setup_conflicts_name_the_setting_and_preserve_existing_native_configuration]` runs six conflict shapes: a wrong collector command, a wrong `target-runner`, a non-array `experimental`, a non-table `scripts`, a non-array profile `scripts`, and a conflicting existing `run-wrapper` rule. For each it asserts the error names the setting and `.config/nextest.toml`, and that the file is unchanged.\n- `fn[native_settings_inheritance_and_precedence]` also checks a conflicting default-profile wrapper rule.\n- `tests/setup.rs#fn[setup_reports_a_conflicting_nextest_wrapper_without_writing_project_files]` runs the real CLI. It asserts a non-zero exit, stderr naming the file and `scripts.wrapper.habeas-coverage`, and that the config, `book.toml`, `SUMMARY.md` and `Cargo.toml` are unchanged.\n\nI found no obligation, boundary or failure case in the text that lacks a test with an assertion. The citations of `requirements.test-coverage.run` and `requirements.test-coverage.processes` are context only, and the routing obligation is covered through `check`. The acknowledgments list is empty, and none is needed.",
  "references": "96b720306e7c96652a5898cfb92a56832cb17c63aaeae24e722eaab32c461e25",
